tree-sitter-yaml: serialize an indentation pair only when it fits

serialize writes ten bytes of state and then four bytes for each open
indentation level, for as long as fewer than 1024 bytes are written. The
last pair can start at byte 1022 and end at byte 1026, past the 1024 bytes
tree-sitter gives a scanner's state: 254 nested block mappings do it.
With its assertions on, tree-sitter's parser aborts the process on the
length the scanner returns; without them, the bytes past the buffer are
overwritten.

A pair is written only when all four of its bytes fit, so the state holds
253 levels and deeper nesting parses as an error.

Applies to src/scanner.c of tree-sitter-yaml at commit
7708026449bed86239b1cd5bce6e3c34dbca6415.

diff --git a/src/scanner.c b/src/scanner.c
index 7168d5380dccf7a6559f5aea3991edb58385e805..8d2bd34a242a3c624718e61f62e1645d33880ffd 100644
--- a/src/scanner.c
+++ b/src/scanner.c
@@ -177,7 +177,10 @@ static unsigned serialize(Scanner *scanner, char *buffer) {
     int16_t *typ_itr = scanner->ind_typ_stk.contents + 1;
     int16_t *typ_end = scanner->ind_typ_stk.contents + scanner->ind_typ_stk.size;
     int16_t *len_itr = scanner->ind_len_stk.contents + 1;
-    for (; typ_itr != typ_end && size < TREE_SITTER_SERIALIZATION_BUFFER_SIZE; ++typ_itr, ++len_itr) {
+    // Each pair takes four bytes; one that would end past the buffer is left
+    // out, with every pair after it.
+    for (; typ_itr != typ_end && size + 2 * sizeof(int16_t) <= TREE_SITTER_SERIALIZATION_BUFFER_SIZE;
+         ++typ_itr, ++len_itr) {
         *(int16_t *)&buffer[size] = *typ_itr;
         size += sizeof(int16_t);
         *(int16_t *)&buffer[size] = *len_itr;
